    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it feels like those \"reframing\" arguments are just excuses at this point. if the evidence is that strong, isn't it kind of misleading to treat both sides as equally valid? like, shouldn't an objective analysis just conclude that the politician is guilty of being dishonest rather than entertaining every possible way they might try to wiggle out of it?",
